## Cross-area non-negotiables

Replace this section with the 3-7 rules that are non-negotiable across
**every** area of your codebase. Examples from the source repos:

### N1. Architecture boundary (per preset)

If you installed a preset that defines an architectural rule (hex
direction, FSD layers, …), reference its rule file here. e.g.:

> Every Go service follows the import direction
> `cmd → adapters → usecase → ports → domain`. Run
> `make verify-isolation` before commit. Full rule:
> [`.claude/rules/hex-boundaries.md`](.claude/rules/hex-boundaries.md).

### N2. Contract-first for cross-service changes

Cross-service contracts (events, REST API shape) MUST change first, in
a separate commit, before any downstream code edits. Code follows
contracts, not the reverse. See
[`docs/playbooks/contract-first.md`](docs/playbooks/contract-first.md).

### N3. 6-gate post-delegation review (MANDATORY)

Every coding subagent that returns MUST pass 6 gates before merge.
**Read [`docs/playbooks/post-delegation-review.md`](docs/playbooks/post-delegation-review.md) for the full playbook.**

1. **Inspect** — `git diff --stat` + read the diff (don't trust the
   subagent's summary)
2. **Build + Test** — real build + real test in every touched area
3. **Boundary** — preset-specific architectural check
4. **Quality (parallel)** — `pr-review-toolkit:{code-reviewer,
   silent-failure-hunter, type-design-analyzer}` (+
   `:pr-test-analyzer` if tests touched)
5. **Wiring (L116)** — composition root has the new code; migrations
   applied; instrumentation emits
6. **Integration smoke** — start the system, run the golden path
   (+ `/design-review` if UI changed)

### N4. Parallel coding conflict prevention (4-layer)

See [`docs/playbooks/parallel-conflict-prevention.md`](docs/playbooks/parallel-conflict-prevention.md). Always: path
declaration → worktree isolation → contract-first → task dependency
graph.

### N5. Test-first discipline

Every implementation task starts with a failing test
(`superpowers:test-driven-development`). No "tests after" — the
failing-first step is what makes the test meaningful.

### N6. Separation of Duties

For regulated work (auth, secrets, RBAC, financial, anything in
scope of SOC2 / HIPAA / FedRAMP / SOX), gate 4 reviewer findings
MUST be acknowledged by a human approver named in the PR's
`PR-APPROVER:` metadata trailer. The approver cannot be the agent
or person who authored the code. CODEOWNERS gates the right team is
involved; the trailer records the named human. See
[`docs/setup/separation-of-duties.md`](docs/setup/separation-of-duties.md).

> Add N7, N8… as your project demands. Keep to ~7 max.

## Workflow (Discovery → Sprint → Design → Implement → Review → Retro)

End-to-end pipeline: [`docs/setup/workflow-master.md`](docs/setup/workflow-master.md).
Stages + driver skills + artifacts + bound rules in one table.

Auto-loaded hot rules: [`.claude/rules/brain-hot.md`](.claude/rules/brain-hot.md).
Mechanical "if touching X → apply Y": [`docs/setup/lesson-trigger-map.md`](docs/setup/lesson-trigger-map.md).

Canonical skills by stage:

| Stage | Skill | Artifact |
|---|---|---|
| Discovery | `/discover` | `docs/spec/discovery/D###-slug.md` |
| Promote backlog → sprint | `/promote` | `docs/spec/sprints/sprint-S<N>.md` row |
| Pick next task | `/next-task` | (selects from sprint file) |
| Author D-doc | `design-doc-writer` agent | `docs/designs/sprint-S<N>/D<NNN>-<slug>.md` |
| Single foreground dispatch | `Agent()` directly | code + tests |
| Parallel fanout | `/dispatch-parallel` | N parallel commits in worktrees |
| 6-gate post-dispatch review | `/post-delegation-gate` | review log |
| UI design fidelity gate | `/design-review` | `docs/spec/reviews/sprint-S<N>-design-review.md` |
| Mid-sprint progress | `/progress` | (status print) |
| Live per-task retro | append manually or `/retro --task` | `docs/spec/retros/sprint-S<N>-tasks.md` |
| Sprint close + audit | `/retro` | `docs/spec/retros/sprint-S<N>.md` |
| Archive old sprint files | `/archive` | move to `sprints/historical/` |

## Sources of truth + cadence

- **Active sprint**: [`docs/spec/STATUS.md`](docs/spec/STATUS.md)
  (single-pane glance — A008)
- **Backlog**: [`docs/spec/backlog.md`](docs/spec/backlog.md)
- **Task spec**: every task gets a design doc at
  `docs/designs/sprint-S<N>/D<NNN>-<slug>.md` BEFORE implementation
  (A005)
- **Live mini-retros**:
  `docs/spec/retros/sprint-S<N>-tasks.md` — append after each task
  closes (A009)
- **Delegation**: dispatch via `Agent` tool with `subagent_type=...`
  (see routing below). **Never `claude -p`** (A006)

## Subagent dispatch routing

| If the task is… | Use `subagent_type` | Reads first |
|---|---|---|
| Pick next task / orchestrate a sprint phase | `{{AGENT_PREFIX}}-orchestrator` | `docs/spec/STATUS.md` + backlog |
| Author a ≥500-line design doc | `design-doc-writer` | task brief + relevant area CLAUDE.md |
| Cross-service design review | `senior-tech-lead` | task design doc + relevant area CLAUDE.md |
| Sprint close + retro authoring | `sprint-retro-author` | sprint files + live mini-retros |
| _(preset agents appear here once installed — see `.claude/agents/`)_ | | |
| Open-ended research / multi-file exploration | `Explore` (built-in) | as needed |
| Code review (general quality) | `pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer` | the diff |
| Silent failure check | `pr-review-toolkit:silent-failure-hunter` | the diff |
| Type design quality | `pr-review-toolkit:type-design-analyzer` | the diff |
| Test coverage gap | `pr-review-toolkit:pr-test-analyzer` | the diff |
| Architectural plan | `feature-dev:code-architect` | relevant CLAUDE.md + design specs |

## Routing the user's request

| If the user asks about… | Read first |
|---|---|
| First-time setup / "how do I start using this" | run `/onboard` (8-stage wizard) — see `docs/setup/onboarding-guide.md` |
| Start a new sprint / pick next task | `docs/spec/STATUS.md` + `docs/spec/backlog.md` → `/next-task` |
| Add a new feature | the relevant area CLAUDE.md → `/promote` → `/next-task` |
| Review a UI sprint / catch "green tests but wrong UI" | `/design-review` |
| Sprint retro / sprint close | `/retro` |
| Deploy / release | `docs/setup/deployment-workflow.md` + `/deploy` |
| Local dev setup | this file `## Quick start` + project README |

